insider_own":12.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Harmonic Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides broadband access solutions worldwide. The company provides software-based broadband access solution, including cOS software-based broadband access solutions to broadband operators, an end-to-end solution consisting of virtualized cloud-native software; hardware products include Oyster, Ripple and SeaStar DAA nodes; Reef and Wave PHY shelf products; pebble remote PHY Devices; and fin, pearl and pier OLT modules and devices; and cOS software-based broadband access solutions to broadband operators; and cOS central cloud services, a subscription service for cOS customers. It also provides technical support and professional services, such as maintenance and support, consulting, implementation, integration services, program management, technical design and planning, building and site preparation, integration and equipment installation, end-to-end system testing, and training, as well as SaaS-related support and deployment. It sells its products through its direct sales force, as well as through independent resellers and systems integrators. It also serves cable and telco operators. The company was incorporated in 1988 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Nimrod  Ben-Natan | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 566 people. Revenue per employee of $637K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $171K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $56K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Harmonic Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.1B market cap on $361M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 50% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $97M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Valued at a 28% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors May Respond To Harmonic (HLIT) Stronger Earnings Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-hlit/harmonic/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-harmonic-hlit-stronger-earnings","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794331672.904,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (HLIT) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/Price-Driven_Insight_from_HLIT_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110926050602_1794218762.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794218762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Harmonic (HLIT) On Strong Q3 Results And 2026 Guidance Still Looks Undervalued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-hlit/harmonic/news/harmonic-hlit-on-strong-q3-results-and-2026-guidance-still-l","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794046745.429,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.946,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Quickline AG Implements Harmonic's cOS Virtual